<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <title>Treasury cubes — scratch</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"/>
  <script src="https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div class="header-top">
    <p class="navline"><a href="index.html">cubes</a> · <a href="data.html">data</a> · <a href="methodology.html">methodology</a> · scratch</p>
    <a class="gh-badge" href="https://github.com/JakeVestal/peachyhabanero" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <h1>SCRATCH</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Local only. Gitignored. Characteristic series only. No published Fed
      plot yet. Long rates = ACM 10y term premium. Employment = NROU − UNRATE
      (up = mandate looking met). Inflation = PCE yoy − 2.
    </p>
    <p class="sub" id="stamp">loading raw_inputs.json…</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Long rates — ACM 10y term premium</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      THREEFYTP10. What duration charges beyond the expected path of funds
      and inflation. Candidate characteristic series for the long-rate mandate.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-acm"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Companions — not the axis</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="sub"><b>DGS10</b> — nominal 10y. Headline long rate. Mixes path + inflation + premium.</p>
        <div id="plot-dgs10"></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="sub"><b>DFII10</b> — 10y TIPS real yield. Board language, still mixed.</p>
        <div id="plot-dfii10"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:16px">
      <p class="sub"><b>T5YIFR</b> — 5y5y forward inflation. Anchoring check, belongs with prices not duration.</p>
      <div id="plot-t5yifr"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Employment — NROU − UNRATE</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Characteristic series for maximum employment. Positive: unemployment
      below CBO natural rate — mandate looks met. Negative: slack. NROU is
      quarterly; held across the months in the quarter. Not a payroll print.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-ugap"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Inflation — PCE yoy − 2%</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      12-month % change in <b>PCEPI</b> minus 2. Official FOMC target from
      January 2012. Pre-2012 is the same 2% applied as today’s lens, not a
      historical Committee target. Adjustable pre-2012 target comes later.
      Up = above target = price-stability mandate missed.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-pigap"></div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:16px"><b>PCE yoy</b> — the raw 12-month rate. Dotted line at 2%.</p>
    <div id="plot-pceyoy"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Treasury stock mix — MSPD original class</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Monthly share of marketable debt <b>held by the public</b> from MSPD
      Table 1. Y is original security class, not remaining maturity.
      A 10-year with eleven months left still sits on Notes. Bills / notes
      / bonds / TIPS / FRN sum toward 1. FRNs are missing-as-zero before
      2014. This is the time-varying mix we already download; the cube
      still uses bills + a 2:1 prior on the rest. Remaining-life CUSIPs
      are not in this plot.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-mix3d" style="min-height:520px"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Remaining maturity — MSPD Table 3</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Same book, different Y. Each CUSIP’s weight sits in
      <b>remaining</b> life: 0–1y, 1–3y, 3–7y, 7–10y, 10y+, plus TIPS and
      FRN off to the side. A 10-year with eleven months left is in 0–1y.
      Amounts are Table 3 outstanding (issued if outstanding is null).
      Not held-by-the-public — Table 3 is total marketable outstanding.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-resid3d" style="min-height:520px"></div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:16px">
      <b>marginal_residual</b> = those weights × TB3MS / DGS2 / DGS5 /
      DGS10 / DGS30 / DFII10 / FEDFUNDS. Cube still uses bills + 2:1
      until we swap it. Months with TIPS weight and no DFII10 print
      are left blank (no fallback).
    </p>
    <div id="plot-marg-compare"></div>
    <div id="plot-refi-compare" style="margin-top:16px"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Robustness — auction $ vs MSPD bills share</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Reminder: the published refi axis uses <b>MSPD bills / marketable stock</b>,
      then 2:1 DGS2:DGS10 on the rest. Auction dollars are the <i>flow that
      actually rolled this quarter</i> — bills turn over faster than the stock
      share, so a referee will ask whether the warn face moves. This plot is
      that check. It is not the cube. Do not promote it until the mapping
      from every security type to TB3MS/DGS2/DGS10 is written down and
      incomplete quarters are allowed to go missing (no fallback).
    </p>
    <div id="plot-auction-share"></div>
    <div id="plot-auction-refi" style="margin-top:16px"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the FOMC did — target range and Δ</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Instrument, not a mandate axis. Band is <b>DFEDTARL–DFEDTARU</b> (range
      from Dec 2008). Line is <b>FEDFUNDS</b>. Markers are month-end first
      difference of the upper bound: magenta hike, lime cut. Holds are the
      months with no marker. Pre-2008 there is no range in this pull —
      only effective funds.
    </p>
    <div id="plot-fomc"></div>
    <div id="plot-delta"></div>
  </section>

  <footer>scratch · peachyhabanero · not deployed</footer>
  <script src="scratch.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
